    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repo, and the full `mvn test` run compiles the whole project and passes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI made `householdId` deterministic from `(normalizedLastName, postcode)` and reworked everything that keys off the household to use it. Changes, each kept in the class that owns that responsibility:\n\n**`OwnerHouseholds`** (the single household definition)\n- `householdId(lastName, postcode)` now hashes `canonical(lastName) + \"|\" + postcode` \u2192 first 12 hex of SHA-256 (was `lastName + \" \" + address`, and only assigned on opt-in).\n- `members(owners, lastName, postcode)` returns existing owners whose own `(lastName, postcode)` hash to the same id \u2014 a robust, order-independent membership test used by every consumer.\n- Removed the now-obsolete `assignedId(...)` opt-in logic.\n\n**`AssignOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 now simply stamps `owner.setHouseholdId(householdId(lastName, postcode))` unconditionally. No repository, no back-filling (determinism makes it unnecessary).\n\n**`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`** \u2014 counts household members via `OwnerHouseholds.members(...)` so the size input keys off the computed household.\n\n**`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity` \u2192 renamed `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 the \"duplicate block\" now rejects (409) when an existing owner shares the household, **unless** `sharesHousehold` is set (which bypasses the block so the owner is created as a declared member). Renamed for accuracy, and the pipeline YAML step (`rejectDuplicateHousehold`) updated to match.\n\n**`AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is now exempted, so a declared member is not flagged as a suspected duplicate.\n\n**Supporting cleanups** \u2014 `DuplicateOwnerException` message/Javadoc, `OwnerIdentity` Javadoc (it no longer drives the reject step, only the response field), and the OpenAPI descriptions for `sharesHousehold`/`householdId` all updated to reflect last-name+postcode and deterministic assignment.\n\n`sharesHousehold` no longer creates the link (that's automatic now) \u2014 it only bypasses the duplicate block, exactly as specified.",
